<title>SINGAPORE: MidEast crude term prices update -- Oman prices.</title>
<headline>MidEast crude term prices update -- Oman prices.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oman has raised the term price of its crude to $19.25 per barrel for May liftings from $17.53 in April, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>Oman became the second Middle East country to announce its official selling prices in the latest round of monthly prices.</p>
<p>Abu Dhabi National Oil Co (ADNOC) announced its retroactive May prices on Sunday.</p>
<p>The following table shows the latest official selling prices and their differential to the quoted Dubai average price for May, which traders use a a gauge of relative value.  </p>
<p>				 (Prices are per barrel)</p>
<p>						   Differential to Dubai</p>
<p>		  May     April   Change   May     April   Change</p>
<p>OMAN	    $19.25  $17.53  +$1.72   +$0.70  +$0.90  (-$0.20)</p>
<p>MURBAN	  $20.00  $18.30  +$1.70   +$1.45  +$1.67  (-$0.22)</p>
<p>LOWER ZAKUM   $20.05  $18.35  +$1.70   +$1.50  +$1.72  (-$0.22)</p>
<p>UMM SHAIF     $19.75  $18.05  +$1.70   +$1.20  +$1.42  (-$0.22)</p>
<p>UPPER ZAKUM   $18.70  $16.70  +$2.00   +$0.15  +$0.07  (+$0.08)</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
